{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And if a man strikes.</b> There is no doubt that the law of an Israelite — whether free or sold — is equal in all matters of law. Therefore it is impossible for this to be a Hebrew slave, and furthermore, for in the latter verse it is written that his money is his. Now, this slave and the maidservant are those whom the verse refers to: of them you may acquire slave and maidservant (Leviticus 25:44). And it opens with bet — a rod — which was his practice to strike them with. Now, all who disagree with our Sages will perforce rely on them regarding the word נקם ינקם, for vengeance is in many ways. But their reasoning will not avail them in this place. And the Fathers received that this is like a sword that avenges the vengeance of the covenant (Leviticus 26:25):"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:59.565277519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}